+/**
+ * Distributor workspace information architecture — spec
+ * `.ai/specs/2026-09-18-distributor-margin-workspace.md`, Deliverable D.
+ *
+ * Page overrides are the only mechanism that re-homes a page into a different sidebar group:
+ * menu injection only appends new groups, and sidebar preferences cannot move an item across a
+ * group boundary. Because `overrides.routes.pages` is keyed globally by path
+ * (`packages/shared/src/modules/overrides.ts` → `applyPageOverridesToManifests`), this app-side
+ * block regroups pages owned by `@open-mercato/core` and `@open-mercato/pricing-engine` without
+ * editing either package.
+ *
+ * The grouping axis is HOW OFTEN a wholesale operator opens a screen, not which engine owns it.
+ * The previous revision grouped by domain and produced sidebar headings that promised work and
+ * delivered rate tables — a group called "Delivery" that held fuel prices and vehicle fuel
+ * consumption and not one delivery. A heading that lies is worse than no heading, because the
+ * operator pays the click before learning it. Three tiers replace it:
+ *   - `daily` — the sell-and-ship loop, in the order the day runs it.
+ *   - `records` — the ledgers that loop reads from: who buys, what is sold, what is in stock.
+ *   - `pricingSettings` — every rate table, in one drawer, last, named for what it holds.
+ * `claims` keeps its own heading: warranty work is real work, just not every day.
+ *
+ * `groupKey` becomes the sidebar group id and is looked up in `apps/mercato/src/i18n/*.json`;
+ * `group` is the literal a locale without that key falls back to, so it stays English.
+ *
+ * `priority` has to be restated per page: `resolveNavItemWeight` reads `priority ?? order`, and
+ * every page in these modules already declares a single per-module priority, which collapses the
+ * declared `order` values and leaves the group sorted alphabetically by title.
+ */
+type DistributorNavPage = {
+  path: string
+  priority: number
+}
