+/**
+ * The dashboard GET seeds a default layout for anyone who has none. Two defects are
+ * covered here:
+ *
+ *  1. A layout row storing zero positions used to be indistinguishable from "the user
+ *     wants nothing", so the defaults were never seeded again and the dashboard stayed
+ *     blank next to a registry full of widgets — repairable only by deleting the row.
+ *  2. The seed followed registry order, so widgets contributed by an app module always
+ *     landed below the core widgets. `metadata.defaultPriority` now orders the seed and
+ *     the picker, while widgets without the hint keep their registry order.
+ *
+ * MEASURED BASELINE — every test below carries one of two labels, because the two are not
+ * the same kind of evidence and were once confused for each other:
+ *
+ *   [PROOF OF FIX]      fails against the pre-fix `route.ts` (the shipped 0.7.0 file, i.e.
+ *                       registry-ordered `allowedWidgets` and a seed guarded by `!layout`).
+ *   [REGRESSION GUARD]  passes against that same pre-fix file. It pins behaviour the fix
+ *                       must not break — it is NOT evidence that either defect was fixed.
+ *
+ * The labels were established by running this file against the pre-fix route with `../route`
+ * remapped to it (`moduleNameMapper`), not by reading the code. Re-measure the same way after
+ * changing a label.
+ */
